{
  "id": "media.config-change-mid-stream",
  "category": "media-plane",
  "spec_cite": [
    "docs/wire-protocol-v2/spec.md §5.2 (PLAYING: decode-affecting config change -> generation +1, push ConfigurationPublished)",
    "docs/wire-protocol-v2/spec.md §7.1 (flags: CONFIG_CHANGE on the first datagram of a greater generation)",
    "docs/wire-protocol-v2/spec.md §7.5 (superseded generation: drop, count unknown_config_drops)",
    "docs/wire-protocol-v2/spec.md §7.6 (unknown configuration: bounded hold, then drop)"
  ],
  "description": "Decode-affecting change mid-stream (48 kHz -> 96 kHz): generation increments 1 -> 2 inside the SAME instance, the reliable ConfigurationPublished push announces it, and media switches generation — including a stale gen-1 datagram that must be dropped, never decoded with either config.",
  "preconditions": [
    "Session PLAYING; instance 1; 30 frames per datagram (240 B F32LE stereo).",
    "The reliable control push and the unreliable datagrams have NO cross-channel ordering guarantee — that is why media carries its generation (§7.2)."
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "kind": "frame",
      "index": 1,
      "dir": "S->C",
      "channel": "control-stream",
      "message": "configuration_published",
      "frame_hex": "00000013aa0210120e080210011a080880ee0510021801",
      "body_hex": "aa0210120e080210011a080880ee0510021801",
      "length": 19,
      "decoded": {
        "request_id": 0,
        "configuration": {
          "config_generation": 2,
          "codec": 1,
          "pcm": {
            "sample_rate": 96000,
            "channels": 2,
            "sample_format": 1
          }
        }
      },
      "has_unknown_fields": false,
      "expect_decode": "ok",
      "note": "Push: config_generation 2, 96 kHz. May arrive before or after the gen-2 datagrams."
    },
    {
      "kind": "datagram",
      "index": 2,
      "dir": "S->C",
      "channel": "datagram",
      "datagram_hex": "",
      "length": 264,
      "decoded": {
        "stream_instance_id": 1,
        "config_generation": 1,
        "sequence": 41,
        "timestamp": 1200,
        "flags": "0x00000000",
        "flags_set": [],
        "payload_bytes": 240,
        "payload_frames": 30,
        "frame_bytes": 8
      },
      "note": "Last normal gen-1 datagram."
    },
    {
      "kind": "datagram",
      "index": 3,
      "dir": "S->C",
      "channel": "datagram",
      "datagram_hex": "",
      "length": 264,
      "decoded": {
        "stream_instance_id": 1,
        "config_generation": 2,
        "sequence": 42,
        "timestamp": 1230,
        "flags": "0x00000002",
        "flags_set": [
          "CONFIG_CHANGE"
        ],
        "payload_bytes": 240,
        "payload_frames": 30,
        "frame_bytes": 8
      },
      "note": "First gen-2 datagram: CONFIG_CHANGE set; generation field is authoritative."
    },
    {
      "kind": "datagram",
      "index": 4,
      "dir": "S->C",
      "channel": "datagram",
      "datagram_hex": "",
      "length": 264,
      "decoded": {
        "stream_instance_id": 1,
        "config_generation": 1,
        "sequence": 43,
        "timestamp": 1260,
        "flags": "0x00000000",
        "flags_set": [],
        "payload_bytes": 240,
        "payload_frames": 30,
        "frame_bytes": 8
      },
      "note": "Stale reorder: gen-1 datagram arriving after gen-2 — drop, count unknown_config_drops."
    },
    {
      "kind": "datagram",
      "index": 5,
      "dir": "S->C",
      "channel": "datagram",
      "datagram_hex": "",
      "length": 264,
      "decoded": {
        "stream_instance_id": 1,
        "config_generation": 2,
        "sequence": 44,
        "timestamp": 1290,
        "flags": "0x00000000",
        "flags_set": [],
        "payload_bytes": 240,
        "payload_frames": 30,
        "frame_bytes": 8
      },
      "note": "Normal gen-2 datagram."
    }
  ],
  "assertions": [
    "config_generation +1 per decode-affecting change (sample_rate/channels/sample_format/codec) within the instance (§7.2); identical content keeps the generation.",
    "The stale gen-1 datagram (step 4) is dropped and counted in unknown_config_drops — never decoded with the previous generation (§7.5); it is NOT decoded under gen 1 either.",
    "If a gen-2 datagram arrives before ConfigurationPublished, it is HELD (never decoded): <= 100 ms or <= 32 datagrams, overflow drops oldest; still unknown after 2 s -> Error(403)+Close(403) (§7.6).",
    "CONFIG_CHANGE is a fast-path hint only; the generation field is authoritative (§7.1).",
    "Sequence and timestamps continue across the change (per-instance counters, §7.1/§7.2)."
  ]
}
